    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 1 Latlurcan, Old Armagh Road, Monaghan is a substantial and spacious five-bedroom, semi-detached residence, with two gardens, extending to approximately 186 m2 (c.2,000 ft2), offering generous and versatile accommodation, over two floors. This substantial property provides an excellent balance of reception, living and bedroom accommodation, in a key location, making it ideally suited for modern family living.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance lobby and spacious hallway, a well-proportioned kitchen, two generous reception rooms and a separate office, together with a utility area and convenient guest W.C.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nA particular feature of the property is the excellent scale of the principal living accommodation, providing an impressive space for both family living and entertaining. The separate sitting room and living room offer valuable additional reception space, while the dedicated office provides an ideal home-working environment, study or maybe a flexible 6th bedroom.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAt first-floor level, the property offers five well-proportioned bedrooms, including an impressive primary bedroom. The remaining bedrooms provide excellent flexibility for family accommodation, guests, children or further home-working requirements. A centrally positioned family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe property is ideally positioned, with the Monaghan Greenway and The Hillgrove Hotel and Leisure Club situated immediately opposite, placing this excellent walking and cycling amenity along with leisure centre facilities on the doorstep. The property also enjoys a particularly attractive setting beside St Macartan’s Cathedral, with views of the Cathedral from the gardens, a number of the bedrooms and on the approach to the property. The property is within easy walking distance of Monaghan Town centre and is also located close to the N2 National Dublin/Derry route, providing excellent connectivity for commuters and those travelling further afield.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from its position on Old Armagh Road, within the established Latlurcan area of Monaghan Town. The mature residential surroundings provide an attractive setting, with the property enjoying a well-established backdrop of neighbouring homes, mature trees and greenery.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe generous proportions, mature setting and excellent range of amenities on the doorstep will appeal to a wide range of purchasers seeking a substantial family residence in a convenient and well-established location close to Monaghan Town centre.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe property may also be eligible for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant and SEAI energy upgrade grants, subject to the property and applicant meeting the relevant eligibility criteria and the terms and conditions of the respective schemes. These grants may provide an opportunity for purchasers to undertake refurbishment and energy-efficiency improvements to the property.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nGround Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Lobby                      2.61m x 1.08m                       \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nEntrance Hall                         \r\n\r\nSpacious entrance hall with access to all principal reception rooms, kitchen and staircase to first floor.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nKitchen                                   5.30m x 3.01m\r\n\r\nWell-proportioned kitchen, with range of fitted units and ample workspace.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOffice                                      4.51m x 3.23m\r\n\r\nUseful home office/study, ideal for working from home, or as a 6th bedroom.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSitting Room                          4.51m x 3.65m\r\n\r\nComfortable front reception room, offering a versatile additional living space.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nLiving / Dining Room             8.45m x 4.88m\r\n\r\nExceptionally spacious principal reception room, ideal as a large family living and entertaining room. Double doors exit on to, the enclosed, side garden and patio.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nRear Lobby / Utility                2.61m x 2.02m\r\n\r\nTiled flooring and half-height wooden panelling to wall\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nGuest W.C.                              1.74m x 0.93m\r\n\r\nConveniently positioned off the utility, adjacent the rear external door.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding\r\n\r\nCentral landing providing access to all bedrooms and bathroom.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBedroom 1                              3.01m x 3.00m\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBedroom 2                              4.51m x 3.23m\r\n\r\nSpacious double bedroom.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBedroom 3                              4.51m x 3.65m\r\n\r\nSpacious double bedroom.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBedroom 4                              3.01m x 2.80m\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBedroom 5                              4.88m x 4.61m\r\n\r\nSpacious double bedroom, with lovely aspect.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBathroom                               2.11m x 1.86m\r\n\r\n Comprising; an electric shower enclosure, W.C., wash hand basin and towel radiator. Modern finish, with ceramic & pvc walling and decorative t&g pvc ceiling.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nExternals\r\n\r\nOff-street parking and Detached garage"
      },
